            <ArticleTitle>Serving, Following, and Leading in Health Care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>603-617</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Radiologic technologists often perform diverse roles throughout the workday, and they should have at least a minimal understanding of the responsibility and effects of these roles on the patient and organization. Although technologists can practice independently or as part of a work group, individuals should be prepared to improve patient care and to function as a servant, follower, and leader for the overall success of the organization. This article examines those roles, emphasizing servantship.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>©2017 American Society of Radiologic Technologists.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
